In short, a KV cache stores intermediate key (K) and value (V) computations=
 for reuse during inference (after training), which results in a substantia=
l speed-up when generating text. The downside of a KV cache is that it adds=
 more complexity to the code, increases memory requirements (the main reaso=
n I initially didn't include it in the book), and can't be used during trai=
ning. However, the inference speed-ups are often well worth the trade-offs =
in code complexity and memory when using LLMs in production.</p><h2 class=
