></div></h3><p><span>Next, we extend the </span><code>forward</code><span> =
method of the </span><code>MultiHeadAttention</code><span> class to accept =
a </span><code>use_cache</code><span> argument:</span></p><pre><code>def fo=
rward(self, x, use_cache=3DFalse):
    b, num_tokens, d_in =3D x.shape
=E2=80=8B
    keys_new =3D self.W_key(x)  # Shape: (b, num_tokens, d_out)
    values_new =3D self.W_value(x)
    queries =3D self.W_query(x)
    #...
=E2=80=8B
    if use_cache:
        if self.cache_k is None:
            self.cache_k, self.cache_v =3D keys_new, values_new
        else:
            self.cache_k =3D torch.cat([self.cache_k, keys_new], dim=3D1)
            self.cache_v =3D torch.cat([self.cache_v, values_new], dim=3D1)
        keys, values =3D self.cache_k, self.cache_v
    else:
        keys, values =3D keys_new, values_new</code></pre><p>The storage an=
d retrieval of keys and values here implements the core idea of the KV cach=
e.</p><p><strong>Storing</strong></p><p><span>Concretely, after the cache i=
s initialized via the if </span><code>self.cache_k is None: ...</code><span=
>, we add the newly generated keys and values via </span><code>self.cache_k=
 =3D torch.cat(...)</code><span> and </span><code>self.cache_v =3D torch.ca=
t(...)</code><span> to the cache, respectively.</span></p><p><strong>Retrie=
ving</strong></p><p><span>Then, </span><code>keys, values =3D self.cache_k,=
 self.cache_v</code><span> retrieves the stored values and keys from the ca=
che.</span></p><p>And that's basically it: the core store &amp; retrieve me=
chanism of a KV cache. The following sections, 3 and 4, just take care of m=
inor implementation details.</p><h3 class=3D"header-anchor-post"><strong>3.=
