07l1.71-1.71"></path></svg></button></div></div></h3><p><span>When generati=
ng text, we have to remember to reset both the keys and value buffers betwe=
en two separate text-generation calls. Otherwise, the queries of a new prom=
pt will attend to stale keys left over from the previous sequence, which ca=
uses the model to rely on irrelevant context and produce incoherent output.=
 To prevent this, we add a </span><code>reset_kv_cache</code><span> method =
to the </span><code>MultiHeadAttention</code><span> class that we can use b=
etween text-generation calls later:</span></p><pre><code>def reset_cache(se=
lf):
    self.cache_k, self.cache_v =3D None, None</code></pre><h3 class=3D"head=
er-anchor-post"><strong>4. Propagating </strong><code>use_cache</code><stro=
ng> in the Full Model</strong><div class=3D"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-ali=
