</div></div></h3><p><span>With the changes to the </span><code>MultiHeadAtt=
ention</code><span> class in place, we now modify the </span><code>GPTModel=
</code><span> class. First, we add a position tracking for the token indice=
s to the instructor:</span></p><pre><code>self.current_pos =3D 0</code></pr=
e><p>This is a simple counter that remembers how many tokens the model has =
already cached during an incremental generation session.</p><p><span>Then, =
we replace the one-liner block call with an explicit loop, passing </span><=
code>use_cache</code><span> through each transformer block:</span></p><pre>=
<code>def forward(self, in_idx, use_cache=3DFalse):
    # ...
=20
    if use_cache:
        pos_ids =3D torch.arange(
            self.current_pos, self.current_pos + seq_len,           =20
            device=3Din_idx.device, dtype=3Dtorch.long
        )
        self.current_pos +=3D seq_len
    else:
        pos_ids =3D torch.arange(
            0, seq_len, device=3Din_idx.device, dtype=3Dtorch.long
        )
   =20
    pos_embeds =3D self.pos_emb(pos_ids).unsqueeze(0)
    x =3D tok_embeds + pos_embeds
    # ...
    for blk in self.trf_blocks:
        x =3D blk(x, use_cache=3Duse_cache)</code></pre><p><span>What happe=
ns above if we set </span><code>use_cache=3DTrue</code><span> is that we st=
art at the </span><code>self.current_pos</code><span> and count </span><cod=
e>seq_len</code><span> steps. Then, bump the counter so the next decoding c=
all continues where we left off.</span></p><p><span>The reason for the </sp=
an><code>self.current_pos</code><span> tracking is that new queries must li=
ne up directly after the keys and values that are already stored. Without u=
sing a counter, every new step would start at position 0 again, so the mode=
l would treat the new tokens as if they overlapped the earlier ones. (Alter=
natively, we could also keep track via an </span><code>offset =3D block.att=
.cache_k.shape[1]</code><span>.)</span></p><p><span>The above change then a=
lso requires a small modification to the </span><code>TransformerBlock</cod=
e><span> class to accept the </span><code>use_cache</code><span> argument:<=
/span></p><pre><code>def forward(self, x, use_cache=3DFalse):
    # ...
    self.att(x, use_cache=3Duse_cache)</code></pre><p><span>Lastly, we add =
a model-level reset to </span><code>GPTModel</code><span> to clear all bloc=
k caches at once for our convenience:</span></p><pre><code>def reset_kv_cac=
he(self):
