div></div></h3><p><span>With the changes to the </span><code>GPTModel</code=
><span>, </span><code>TransformerBlock</code><span>, and </span><code>Multi=
HeadAttention</code><span>, finally, here's how we use the KV cache in a si=
mple text generation function:</span></p><pre><code>def generate_text_simpl=
e_cached(
        model, idx, max_new_tokens, use_cache=3DTrue
    ):
    model.eval()
=E2=80=8B
    ctx_len =3D model.pos_emb.num_embeddings  # max sup. len., e.g. 1024
    if use_cache:
        # Init cache with full prompt
        model.reset_kv_cache()
        with torch.no_grad():
            logits =3D model(idx[:, -ctx_len:], use_cache=3DTrue)
=E2=80=8B
        for _ in range(max_new_tokens):
            # a) pick the token with the highest log-probability=20
            next_idx =3D logits[:, -1].argmax(dim=3D-1, keepdim=3DTrue)
            # b) append it to the running sequence
            idx =3D torch.cat([idx, next_idx], dim=3D1)
            # c) feed model only the new token
            with torch.no_grad():
                logits =3D model(next_idx, use_cache=3DTrue)
    else:
        for _ in range(max_new_tokens):
            with torch.no_grad():
                logits =3D model(idx[:, -ctx_len:], use_cache=3DFalse)
            next_idx =3D logits[:, -1].argmax(dim=3D-1, keepdim=3DTrue)
            idx =3D torch.cat([idx, next_idx], dim=3D1)
=E2=80=8B
    return idx</code></pre><p><span>Note that we only feed the model the ne=
w token in c) via </span><code>logits =3D model(next_idx, use_cache=3DTrue)=
</code><span>. Without caching, we feed the model the whole input </span><c=
ode>logits =3D model(idx[:, -ctx_len:], use_cache=3DFalse)</code><span> as =
it has no stored keys and values to reuse.</span></p><h2 class=3D"header-an=
