</div></h4><p>Rather than concatenating tensors repeatedly, we could pre-al=
locate a sufficiently large tensor based on the expected maximum sequence l=
ength. This ensures consistent memory use and reduces overhead. In pseudo-c=
ode, this may look like as follows:</p><pre><code># Example pre-allocation =
for keys and values
max_seq_len =3D 1024  # maximum expected sequence length
